<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.1.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01738</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.1.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>01dc4264-a624-4477-9ee5-618726fdb629</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will use your knowledge of geometric patterns to create tables and graphs that will represent the area of a garden.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Create drawings, tables, and graphs that represent the area of a garden.</item>
        <item>Recognize a situation represented by a graph that increases and then decreases.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>7.1.1: Noticing New Patterns of Change</item>
        <item>7.1.2: The Relationship Between Length and Area <list id="list-00003">
            <item>7.1.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>7.1.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>7.1.3: Plotting Measurements <list id="list-00004">
            <item>7.1.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>7.1.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>7.1.4: The Input and Output of a Function</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>7.1.5: Practice</item>
        <item>7.1.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
